WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.826
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:09.965
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.265 --> 00:00:19.245
Unit five: Conditionals: Zero, First, Second and Third. Today you will use if sentences for facts, plans and imagined situations.

4
00:00:19.545 --> 00:00:22.302
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:26.407
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.228
Condition.

7
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:32.075
Condition means a situation that must happen first.

8
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:34.149
The condition is simple.

9
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.414
Your turn. Say: Condition.

10
00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:41.082
Condition.

11
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:42.678
Result.

12
00:00:43.683 --> 00:00:45.544
Result means what happens after.

13
00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.453
The result was good.

14
00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.493
Your turn. Say: Result.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.183
Result.

16
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.951
Unless.

17
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.532
Unless means if not.

18
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:01.186
Unless you study, you will fail.

19
00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:04.436
Your turn. Say: Unless.

20
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.440
Unless.

21
00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:10.115
Provided.

22
00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:12.675
Provided means only if.

23
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:15.074
You can go provided you finish.

24
00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:18.336
Your turn. Say: Provided.

25
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.108
Provided.

26
00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:23.886
Imagine.

27
00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.196
Imagine means to picture in your mind.

28
00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:29.295
Imagine you had a car.

29
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:32.745
Your turn. Say: Imagine.

30
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.520
Imagine.

31
00:01:37.283 --> 00:01:38.238
Regret.

32
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.900
Regret means sadness about the past.

33
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:43.717
I have a regret.

34
00:01:44.317 --> 00:01:47.329
Your turn. Say: Regret.

35
00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:50.970
Regret.

36
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:52.567
Probable.

37
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:55.478
Probable means likely to happen.

38
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:57.491
Rain is probable.

39
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:00.503
Your turn. Say: Probable.

40
00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:04.263
Probable.

41
00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:05.983
Unreal.

42
00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:08.716
Unreal means not true now.

43
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:11.154
It is an unreal situation.

44
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.147
Your turn. Say: Unreal.

45
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.048
Unreal.

46
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:22.345
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.183 --> 00:02:25.891
Visal, what are the four conditionals?

48
00:02:26.983 --> 00:02:41.295
Zero is for facts: If you heat ice, it melts. First is for likely futures: If it rains, I will stay home. Second is for unreal present: If I had money, I would travel.

49
00:02:42.383 --> 00:02:43.431
And the third?

50
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:54.727
The third conditional is for unreal past situations: If I had studied, I would have passed. It describes a past regret that cannot change now.

51
00:02:55.817 --> 00:02:57.154
What does unless mean?

52
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:08.254
Unless means if not. Unless you hurry, you will be late means If you do not hurry, you will be late. Do not use a second negative after unless.

53
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.040
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.883 --> 00:03:15.021
Grammar focus: If plus tense, result clause.

55
00:03:15.321 --> 00:03:16.577
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:19.306
If I had money, I would travel.

57
00:03:20.217 --> 00:03:22.901
If I had studied, I would have passed.

58
00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:32.147
Zero uses present + present, first uses present + will, second uses past + would, and third uses past perfect + would have.

59
00:03:32.883 --> 00:03:36.790
Be careful! Don't say: If I will study, I pass.

60
00:03:38.733 --> 00:03:41.046
Say: If I study, I will pass.

61
00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:42.661
No will after if.

62
00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:46.049
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:47.753
If Only.

64
00:03:48.053 --> 00:03:50.471
If it rains tomorrow, we will stay at home.

65
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.942
If I had more money, I would visit Japan.

66
00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:58.047
If Dara had studied harder, he would have passed.

67
00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.207
Unless you hurry, you will miss the bus.

68
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.967
If you heat ice, it melts.

69
00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:09.045
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:09.883 --> 00:04:12.997
Second conditional: If I blank rich, I would travel.

71
00:04:13.297 --> 00:04:16.161
A, am. B, will be. C, were.

72
00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.363
The answer is C: were.

73
00:04:22.517 --> 00:04:25.433
Third: If I had studied, I blank passed.

74
00:04:25.733 --> 00:04:28.853
A, would have. B, will. C, would.

75
00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.156
The answer is A: would have.

76
00:04:35.317 --> 00:04:36.829
Unless means blank.

77
00:04:37.129 --> 00:04:40.306
A, when. B, if not. C, because.

78
00:04:43.867 --> 00:04:45.762
The answer is B: if not.

79
00:04:46.917 --> 00:04:48.997
Zero conditional is for blank.

80
00:04:49.297 --> 00:04:53.113
A, regrets. B, dreams. C, facts.

81
00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.631
The answer is C: facts.

82
00:04:59.783 --> 00:05:02.178
First: If it rains, I blank stay.

83
00:05:02.478 --> 00:05:05.481
A, will. B, would. C, had.

84
00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:10.673
The answer is A: will.

85
00:05:11.867 --> 00:05:15.274
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:16.117 --> 00:05:18.406
Finish: If I had more free time...

87
00:05:27.217 --> 00:05:28.752
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:29.052 --> 00:05:37.779
If I had more free time, I would read more books. I would also practise English every day. I would learn a new language.

89
00:05:38.079 --> 00:05:39.788
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.683 --> 00:05:46.296
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and if plus tense, result clause.

91
00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:51.373
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

92
00:05:51.673 --> 00:05:54.326
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:05:54.626 --> 00:05:58.265
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

